  "description": "RAQWAL crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C76 H112 Cl3 Gd7 N16 O26 2+,2(Cl1 1-),C1 H4 O1,1.75(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 5 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 4 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd7 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.569-4.064 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 92.71-114.91°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C77H119Cl5Gd7N16O29.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
